# What must never enter the build context. Two reasons, and the second is the one that
# matters: a smaller context is faster, but an *excluded secret* is a secret that cannot
# end up in a layer. `.env` is the one that would.
#
# Note the asymmetry with the Dockerfile: this file says what cannot come in, and the
# Dockerfile still COPYs an explicit subset. Both are needed — ADR 0004's addendum is
# the story of `content/` being a build input that the Dockerfile did not copy, which no
# amount of .dockerignore would have caught.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/coverage-gate
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs
spike
playwright-report
test-results
*.log
# M14 tees the API's stdout here for Promtail; never part of an image.
logs
# The local Grafana/Prometheus/Loki profile is compose-only: nothing in the image reads it.
docker/observability
e2e
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.e2e.json
.vscode
.idea
